From 7ce65ab844c500825091aa7249c7059930eecc3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Peshkov <slimstalker@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:31:05 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] nir/opt_preamble: add a can_move_instr_cb option

Backends may only be able to execute a subset of instructions in their
preamble, or executing some instruction there may make the preamble
much more expensive (on Adreno, a single GPR write turns an early
preamble into a late one). The existing callbacks cannot express this:
avoid_instr_cb only stops an instruction from being the root of a
rewrite, it can still be moved as part of a bigger expression.

Add an optional callback which lets the backend keep an instruction,
and everything depending on it, in the main shader.

