+ * when no wave is launched at all, and has no GPRs. So it can only contain
+ * speculatable loads and instructions whose results live in shared registers.
+ * A single instruction that breaks this turns the whole preamble into a late
+ * one, where the first wave executes it while every other wave of the draw
+ * waits. That stall costs far more than hoisting the instruction saves, so on
+ * GPUs with early preamble keep such instructions (and everything derived from
+ * them) in the main shader:
